      {
        "id": 265842,
        "name": "",
        "username": "LonelyMan",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2026-07-09T16:19:22.587Z",
        "cooked": "<p>My pulp superhero alter ego, Doctor Thermocline, really enjoyed the intro banter section.</p>\n<p>Argh!  Dudes!  It’s right there!  Quesedillas, Quandaries and Queries!</p>\n<p>They forgot to mention that Weird is spelled with two Us as well as a Double U.  It’s uuWuUEIrDd!</p>\n<p>Oh, so this story is where the Breaking the Rules art comes from.</p>\n<p>No Guise, no Grimm, no Scholar, no Visionary, not even Aeternus…this story comes as quite a surprise.  I’m glad the First Fear ties into something we knew about while still being new, plus there’s a tease of a Singular Entity behind it.  It’s probably not Sgaedoth, but that’s another one I thought about while trying to guess where it was going.</p>\n<p>Malarkey lol.  I’m astonished that I haven’t heard this word on the podcast before, as far as I recall, considering how often other terms for nonsense get used.</p>\n<p>I cannot possibly express the intensity with which I disagree with the Matilda point.  Forcing me to participate in such a scene would be a worse torture than can be inflicted on me with fewer than three razor blades.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2026-07-09T18:11:56.673Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
